The soothing breeze, whispers of leaves, and an eerily comfortable silence.
A flash of someone's eyes, and then none.

>From a towering stone building comes Lauren, having left after subduing
Olivia and outwitting Brandon. The rain is now a gentle pour, as she
continues her journey back home. Gianna rides on her shoulders as they
venture away from the prison, Natalie a fading memory.

In Tyler's house sits a beautiful dress- it's blue, as is representative of
his persona as indicated by the 2014 Erikson book. The clock strikes
midnight, and suddenly Tyler appears normally again. The dress is nowhere
to be seen. As it's another 4 hours until his bedtime, Tyler resumes
watching videos on how to fold hoodies.

On her way home Lauren is passing by a neighborhood. She deposits Gianna to
her home in a worm hole. Gianna shrinks down to the size of a beetle and
enters her worm hole. Lauren continues walking through the neighborhood.
The rain has slowed to a slight drizzle. Silence fills the air except for
the rustling of grass and the damp steps from Lauren's shoes. She notices a
slight movement from the corner of her eye. From a certain house out comes
Tyler, doing his daily walk at 3am.
"What are *you* doing here?" says Tyler. "This is my turf!"
"No, this is God's turf!" replies Lauren.

Lauren unsheathes her 24ft 14 karat gold sword. She uses the power of her
brain to materialize a wide 99.999% platinum shield. She lets out a sharp
shriek, and a lightning bolt bolts down from the sky, encasing her in a
blinding light. The light retreats, and Lauren is encased in full golden
body armor. She is literally on fire. Lauren is prepared to fight Tyler to
the death.

Tyler has no weapon.

Lauren raises her shield, points her sword at Tyler, and advances towards
him full force. She raises her sword to strike, and Tyler barely dives out
of the way. In the corner of his eye, Tyler sees a very long stick. The
perfect weapon. He just has to get to it first. Lauren swipes her sword
again, aiming for Tyler's head. Tyler rolls out of the way and quickly gets
on his feet. Lauren is blocking the way to the stick. How will he get
there? Tyler has an idea.
"Look! Natalie escaped from the prison!"
Lauren looks back. She is confused.
"What? No she didn't. I left her there."
Tyler sees his chance. He runs past Lauren, the stick just within reach.
But Lauren is too fast. She sees the stick and immediately sees what he is
trying to do. She throws her shield at Tyler and knocks him to the ground.
Lauren slowly approaches, sword raised. She swings her sword and strikes,
but the sword makes contact with the ground. Tyler has turned into a
beautiful blue dress. Lauren missed.

The dress transforms back into Tyler and he grabs the stick and swiftly
backs away. Lauren, enraged, is prepared to strike again. But just as she
raises her sword, it disappears. The fire around her swiftly fades away.
Her shield and armor dissolve into thin air.
Lauren is very confused. She looks at Tyler. "What happened?"
"This is some dark magic. It must be the work of a witch!" exclaims Tyler.
Immediately Lauren thinks of 1 person. She very dramatically turns to
Tyler, a serious look in her eye.
"Olivia." she says very seriously. "We need to find her and destroy her!"

Lauren and Tyler venture off into the forest. They go back to the worm hole
to search for Gianna. They call for Gianna, but nothing emerges from the
hole. Lauren has a brilliant idea, and pulls a piece of kimchi out of her
pocket. She lays the kimchi in front of the hole, planning to lure Gianna
out of the hole. It doesn't take long for Gianna to take the bait. A cute
little small beetle crawls out of the hole and turns into Gianna. They
explain their situation with the dark magic witch Olivia, and Gianna agrees
to help defeat her. But this isn't enough. They need more manpower, more
firepower, more willpower. Lauren has the perfect idea.

The heroic trio sprint their way through the forest, hurdling over fallen
tree trunks and dodging pesky bugs. Gianna occasionally stops to take a
nap, and Lauren has to lay a trail of kimchi so Gianna can catch up after
napping. After traveling for 3 days and 5 nights, the trio decides to make
camp. The sun is beginning to set, and soon darkness will be among them.
Gianna digs a nice hole for herself and nibbles on her last piece of
kimchi. She feels sleepy again, so she turns into a beetle and retreats
deeper into the hole. Tyler climbs a tree and rests on one of the branches.
He turns into a beautiful blue dress and hangs peacefully in the breeze.
Lauren reaches for her sword so she can cut down some fresh branches and
build shelter, but remembers that Olivia the Evil Sorcerer has dissolved
her sword. Lauren slowly lays down on the cold, hard ground and tries to
fall asleep.

A sweet, fruity smell fills the air as the sun's rays begin to peek through
the trees. Music dances past Lauren's ears as she hears the songs of birds
alongside the crisp crackling of a campfire. She looks over to see Tyler
and Gianna resting beside the fire, cooking mysterious red berries.
"Are you sure we can eat those?" questioned Lauren.
Tyler gives her a quizzical look as if this is common knowledge. "Yes, all
mysterious berries are safe to eat."
Lauren does not question Tyler's judgement. Gianna has already eaten
several berries (in beetle form). Lauren grabs a berry off the fire and
plops it in her mouth. The taste is immaculate. She takes possession of all
the berries and downs them all in no more than 5 seconds.
"Alright, let's continue!" exclaims Lauren. The three get up and continue
their journey through the forest. Tyler is sad because he didn't get to eat
any mysterious berries.

The triumphant trio find themselves back at the large stone prison. The
serious guard stands in front, performing his job very seriously. Lauren
makes her way across the moat and confidently approaches the guard.
"We need your help!" Lauren exclaims.
"Sure, I will help!" responds Brandon the Guard. Brandon closes the gate to
the prison, fully prepared to leave his post and help the group. They
desperately need him and he knows it. Brandon will provide the best
willpower to the group. The ferocious four run into the distance, prepared
to bring Olivia down once and for all.

~~ intermission ~~

The four reach the edges of the forest, seeing a large metropolis on the
horizon. A massive cloud looms over the whole city. It is moving slowly,
ominously, in a large spiral. In the center of the spiral, a large
skyscraper reaches up. That is Olivia's fortress. This is where the four
must venture.
Gianna has an undying urge to eat chicken wings. The city is so close- all
they have to do is make a pit stop. Gianna voices her concerns to the
group. "I'm hungry :(" Everyone turns to Gianna and thinks for a bit. They
decide that they need someone to scout out the area anyway, otherwise
they'll be going into the battlefield blind. Tyler volunteers to go map out
the tower and the area around it so he can formulate a plan while the
others get chicken wings. He is very hungry, but he is also still salty
about Lauren eating all the berries. He needs time to cool down.
Tyler turns into a dress and moves like a flying carpet off into the
distance. He is a very stealthy scout. The others venture to another part
of the city in search of chicken wings.


7 hours later, the four regroup at the chicken wing place. Gianna, Lauren,
and Brandon are very satisfied and full with chicken wings. Tyler is
satisfied with a job well done in scouting out Olivia's palace, but he
comes with urgent news. Natalie is being held prisoner in Olivia's tower.
They must formulate a plan to save her!
"What?! Do we have to?" exclaimed Lauren. "She'll be fine."
The others disagree. They must rescue her! They swiftly head out, ready to
stop Olivia once and for all.

The big city skyline looms over everyone. A tense uneasiness over the
population, rumors of some pending crisis, the uneasiness of the current
calm. Natalie is held hostage at the top of 200 Park Ave 10166, and Tyler,
Lauren, and Gianna stand at the bottom, on the road leading from Grand
central station. Brandon quickly goes to the top to try to free Natalie,
but is stopped suddenly. Olivia stands in front of him. "Stop",  she says.
Brandon stops, then immediately runs to save Natalie, "You didn't say how
long". Olivia tackles him violently and puts him in a cage seperate to
Natalie (covid 19 social distancing). Unable to see because it's far away
and two thirds of them are borderline blind Tyler, Lauren, and Gianna stand
at the bottom trying to figure out what to do next.

The tremendous trio bolt up the stairs. They stand face to face with
Olivia, her sorceress staff at the ready. Lauren runs around in circles,
aiming to distract Olivia. Tyler turns into a flying dress and also travels
in circles, also aiming to distract Olivia. Gianna transforms into a
beetle, swiftly enters Brandon's cage, and unlocks it. Brandon begins
shouting words of encouragement as Lauren and Olivia engage in hand-to-hand
combat.
"Give me back my 24ft 14 karat gold sword!" demanded Lauren.
"Never!" politely responded Olivia.

Gianna (still in beetle form) stealthily and swiftly approaches Olivia as
she continues to 1-on-1 battle Lauren. Brandon continues to provide
excellent willpower, and Tyler continues to fly in circles, creating giant
gusts of wind. Lauren kicks Olivia, then grabs Olivia's arm and judo-flips
her over her shoulder. Lauren pins Olivia's shoulders to the ground. She is
trapped. Olivia slowly grabs her staff, ready to unleash a powerful spell.
But just then- SWOOSH! Gianna the Beetle flies through the air and lands in
Olivia's eye.
"AAAHH! A BEETLE!!!" Olivia calmly proclaimed. "Fine! I surrender!"

Lauren helps Olivia up. "SIKE!" Olivia suddenly whips out her staff and
smacks Lauren in the stomach. The battle continues. Brandon is now shouting
even more encouraging words of encouragement, and Tyler speeds up his
circles. Gianna turns back into human form.
"Stop! Can't we all be friends?"
Olivia and Lauren stop fighting for a second. They ponder this for a moment.
"Yes, we should be friends," Olivia says.
Everyone stops fighting and groups together in the center of the room.
Tyler turns back into human form, the winds still blowing in circles.
Lauren, Gianna, Brandon, Tyler, and Olivia all do a group hug. Their issue
is resolved, and Olivia will no longer be an evil sorceress. Hurrah!

Just then Brandon looks back and sees something frightening. A giant
tornado has formed in the room during their group hug. Tyler flew too fast!
The ground begins to rumble, the ceiling cracking and shaking. The building
is going to collapse! The ferocious four quickly make their way out of the
tower. As soon as they reach the ground, pieces of the tower begin hitting
the ground. A sinkhole forms as the tower caves in on itself. Luckily, all
the main characters made it out safely.

*Final scene where olivia is a good guy*

*Everyone hugs and is friends*

The end. Remember to Never Eat Soggy Waffles.

--000000000000d84363061176e636
